content:
Exactly! You want a set where the numbers are packed closer together, meaning the spacing between them is less than 10.

Take a look at the four options:
A: {110, 120, 130, 140, 150}
B: {-50, -40, -30, -20, -10}
C: {15, 20, 25, 30, 35}
D: {0, 20, 40, 60, 80}

Which of these sets has a spacing of less than 10 between its numbers?

Bingo! Set C has a spacing of 5, which means the numbers are clustered closer together than Set X. Therefore, its standard deviation is smaller. 

To really lock this concept in, let's quickly look at Sets A and B:
A: {110, 120, 130, 140, 150}
B: {-50, -40, -30, -20, -10}

Even though the numbers in Set A are much larger, and the numbers in Set B are negative, how do you think their standard deviations compare to Set X?
